Well, I downloaded NetHack 3.1 for my Mac Plus. After noticing
a whole bunch of different files, I wondered what might be different.

Everything, I found out, including the interface.

I personally think that the interface for everything being in a window
was A BAD IDEA. I am a faithful user of the old 3.09 Mac version, and
liked the simple one-window interface. Why couldn't the new 3.1 use the
same interface as the faithful 3.0 versions?

Another problem with NetHack 3.1 I found was the inability to set
options. Who was the genius that made a seperate Options file we would
have to edit ourselves? I used the options I was familiar with from a
network version and my .cshrc. It then bitched at me about how the
Options were set wrong. What was so bad about setting options from
the way they were in 3.0?

The challenge of NetHack 3.1 has me excited. The way NetHack 3.1 is
graphically and interfaced different from it's predecessors sucks.

My recommendations? Take the 3.1 code and program it to be like the
old 3.0 versions of NetHack. Don't get so "window happy" Not everyone
likes a window for attributes, a window for inventories, a window
for this and a window for that. Christ, you'd think Bill Gates was one
of the "supreme deities".

My hope is that the Development team is reading this and getting out
a binary source for 3.09 for the Mac to modify.

PS. Who was the idiot that took out the gold dropping bug? Considering
the difficulties of NetHack, any easter egg like infinite gold can
make the difference between winning and losing. Bring the gold dropping
bug back in 3.1.

